{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Chronicle creation starts with four choices. Manual creation opens a real owned Untitled Chronicle directly in the existing editor; AI, story adaptation and whole-Chronicle templates visibly show Coming soon. Header rename and inline Chronicle Details preserve canonical ownership, save/history, optimistic version checks, retry, conflict recovery and publication validation.\n\n**Draft, unmerged; owner approval recorded, effective Sounding Line exception pending.** Independent review THREE remains BLOCKED by `SC-00A-REVIEW-A11Y-01`: the two desktop complementary landmarks lack distinct accessible names. KG directly approved **PE-X-SC00A-LANDMARKS-20261015** in native human message `01a1423c-7e0c-75e0-aea6-fedd6db3bc08`. The [approval record](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/6309b2d1c587e484a63ded1025faa298b83f3e4e/Development_Docs/Projects/Chronicle_Creator/evidence/sc-00a-review4-exception-20261015/owner-approval.json) preserves that exact decision separately from the original [inactive proposal](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/b305645d0fb60d4e0761dfa812f0ccd5b7674e68/Development_Docs/Projects/Chronicle_Creator/SC_00A_Review_Limit_Exception_Proposal.md) and [structured proposal](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/b305645d0fb60d4e0761dfa812f0ccd5b7674e68/Development_Docs/Projects/Chronicle_Creator/evidence/sc-00a-review4-exception-20261015/exception.proposed.json).\n\nThe existing Sounding Line owner has natively verified the approval and is preparing its narrow canonical authority. The approved [two-label patch](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/b305645d0fb60d4e0761dfa812f0ccd5b7674e68/Development_Docs/Projects/Chronicle_Creator/evidence/proposed-landmark-labels.patch), SHA-256 `d92ff80369604adec514ec9a1bac4393b9a3a2a80d01d42cc78529b190c57e76`, is still unapplied. No fresh capture or review FOUR has started. The finite grant permits only that correction, one fresh trusted source-bound capture attempt and the fourth independent review, through October 22, 2026, 23:59:59 America/New_York (`2026-10-23T03:59:59Z`). Failed/cancelled attempts consume the allowance. Prior review history, ordinary Mainline Decision, protected merge and landed verification remain unchanged. The repaired candidate must reconcile and bind the actual effective protected base.\n\nHistorical product source `d35140129eadae99f8ec0a8eb3f9ff525b50fc59`, on base `99a2babaefbbe051de0352c4aca22c8723b743b8`, passed 29 focused tests, eight production browser cases and four desktop/mobile normal/reduced-motion journeys. Trusted [capture 38688383108](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38688383108) preserves all 40 artifacts; review THREE found the moderate landmark defect despite passing serious/critical axe thresholds. The two measured transient contrast defects were repaired. Earlier ordinary run `38684202576` remains FAILURE, and older accepted iteration-two artifacts remain historical. No current accepted attestation or ordinary PASS is claimed. Documentation and catalog checks pass; capability promotion remains deferred.\n\n[Implementation, qualification and integration handoff](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/6309b2d1c587e484a63ded1025faa298b83f3e4e/Development_Docs/Projects/Chronicle_Creator/SC_00A_Implementation_and_Qualification.md) records source identities, failed receipts, completed capabilities and shared-file ownership. SC-00A owns Chronicle creation, Details, header and TaleEditor changes plus affected browser consumers. Shared testing registrations and generated documentation/catalog files require reconciliation. Canonical schema, authorization, publication and Scene/Environment storage are unchanged; pending SC-01 immutable references remain an owning-task interface.\n\nSC-00's Spatial Studio overhaul remains in its existing chat and PR #722, where the owner's continuation/handoff instructions were routed and acknowledged. SC-00B Inspector/tool rail, SC-00C Library and SC-07A Harborlight publishing remain separate. This PR does not claim those refits, physical devices, live assistive-technology testing or owner PRODUCT_ACCEPTED.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:14:26Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:14:26Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"feat(studio): create Chronicles directly and edit details inline","oid":"a7abce34e689dacbb508a65bc0850506341bf14e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:15:45Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:15:45Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix(studio): limit history reset to explicit conflict recovery","oid":"c3cb87ba1467eef7011dfb687838723f3ebd730e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:18:50Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:18:50Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"refactor(studio): retain the unchanged canonical creation service","oid":"31edca22d7d8b55f3ff1db01a1bf1deeed77b3b6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:20:03Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:20:03Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix(studio): recover manual draft identity after a lost response","oid":"56ad2187d312023b534860572843f5cd676d34ed"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:25:49Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:25:49Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"test(studio): follow Chronicle cards and accessible editor titles","oid":"3ec21eecbbc393cb9f40f130aacfc3b6b36391e9"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:31:46Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6